<mjml>
  <mj-head>
    <mj-font name="Source Sans Pro" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Source+Sans+Pro:200,400,700&display=swap" />

    <!-- defines the style for different tags -->
    <mj-style inline="inline">
      a {
        color: #fbc926; /* Make links this color */
      }
      p {
        margin: 0.2em 0; /* Adjusts vertical spacing */
      }
      h2 {
        text-decoration: underline; /* Adds underline */ margin-bottom: 0.1em; /* Adjust margin below */ color: #ffffff
      }
    </mj-style>
  </mj-head>

  <!-- defines the color of the background that the column of content sits on top of -->
  <mj-body background-color="#222">
    <!-- add an empty section for padding at the top of the email -->
    <mj-section> </mj-section>

    <!--  defines the background color behind the text -->
    <mj-section padding="0" background-color="#000000">
      <mj-column>
        <!-- insert a banner image -->
        <mj-image padding="0" width="600px" src="https://static.presidentscup.us/2025.11.20.hero-banner.png" alt="2026 President's Cup Competition Banner. #PRESCUP" />

        <!-- defines the text style (font and color) -->
        <mj-text font-family="Source Sans Pro, sans-serif" padding-top="20px" font-size="16px" color="#be9206" line-height="1.3">

        </mj-text>

        <mj-text font-family="Source Sans Pro, sans-serif" font-size="16px" color="#ffffff" line-height="1.3">
          <!-- insert email content here -->

          <p>
            {{ name }},
          </p>
          <br />

          <p>
            Congratulations! You have qualified for Individuals Offensive Track Round 2 in the seventh annual President's Cup Cybersecurity Competition. 
          </p>
          <br />
          
          <p>
            Round 2 will be open from <b>February 3, 9:00 AM ET - February 10, 11:59 PM ET.</b> Best of luck!
          </p>
          <br />

          <p>
            *Pro Tip: <b>The timer starts when the first challenge is launched and cannot be paused.</b> You will have <b>four</b> hours to compete once the timer begins.
          </p>
          <br />

          <p>
            Keep your skills sharp by practicing with sample challenges via the <a href="https://pccc.cisa.gov/gb/practice">Practice Area</a>, where you can replay challenges from PC6 and other previous President's Cups.
            You are also encouraged to head over to the <a href="https://github.com/cisagov/prescup-challenges">Github page</a>, where you will find multiple resources such as challenge descriptions and solution guides from the previous competition challenges.            
          </p>
          <br />

          <p>If you have any questions, email us at <a href="mailto:presidentscup@cisa.dhs.gov">presidentscup@cisa.dhs.gov</a>.</p>
        </mj-text>

        <mj-text font-family="Source Sans Pro, sans-serif" font-size="16px" color="#ffffff" line-height="1.3">
          <h3>Support Hours during Qualifying Rounds</h3>
        </mj-text>

        <mj-text font-family="Source Sans Pro, sans-serif" font-size="16px" color="#be9206" line-height="1.3">
          <ul>
            <li>Monday - Friday, 8:00 AM - 11:00 PM ET</li>
            <li>Saturday - Sunday, 9:00 AM - 5:00 PM ET</li>
          </ul>
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text font-family="Source Sans Pro, sans-serif" font-size="16px" color="#ffffff" line-height="1.3">
          <h3>Important Reminder: Rules of Conduct</h3>
          <p>
            As you advance to Round 2, please remember that all competitors are expected to adhere to the President's Cup Rules of Conduct. In particular, we highlight Rule #7:
          </p>

          <blockquote>
            Competitors must not disclose any information about the challenges to anyone outside their competition team during the respective round.
          </blockquote>

          <p>
            Any sharing of challenge details, solutions, or answers with individuals outside your team, or obtaining such information from others prior to or during the competition, is strictly prohibited. Violation of this rule may result in disqualification, and enforcement is at the discretion of the Competition Staff.
          </p>

          <br />

          <p>
            We rely on your professionalism and integrity to ensure a fair and honorable competition for all participants. Please review the full <a href="https://presidentscup.cisa.gov/pc7/">Rules of Conduct</a> on our website and conduct yourself in a manner befitting federal government employees and members of the Uniformed Services.
          </p>

          <br />

          <p>
            Thank you for your cooperation, and good luck in Round 2!
          </p>
        </mj-text>

        <!-- show a button for the prescup site -->
        <mj-button padding-bottom="40px" font-family="Source Sans Pro, sans-serif" href="https://cisa.gov/presidentscup" background-color="#ff0a44" color="#ffffff" font-size="18px"> cisa.gov/<strong>presidentscup</strong> </mj-button>

      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- add an empty section for padding at the bottom of the email -->
    <mj-section> </mj-section>
  </mj-body>
</mjml>
